Start from a feasible multi-order vector \(\mathbf r^{(0)}\). At iteration \(k\), solve the relaxation with bound \(\rho_{\mathbf r^{(k)}}\), compute a refinement score \(s_j^{(k)}\) for each constraint from a prescribed diagnostic, and select a nonempty set \(J_k\). Update \(r_j^{(k+1)}=r_j^{(k)}+1\) for \(j\in J_k\), retain \(r_j^{(k+1)}=r_j^{(k)}\) otherwise, and increase the ambient order if required by degree compatibility. Stop when the bound gap or all selected scores meet a stated tolerance. Output the final bound and order vector; nesting guarantees \(\rho_{
\mathbf r^{(k+1)}}
\ge
\rho_{
\mathbf r^{(k)}}\).
